    "note" : "Given a course's configuration, what deploy.sh is asked to do. One place must decide this in each app — on the mac it is DeployCommand.arguments, shared by the Deploy button, the assistant and the scheduled-deploy alarm. Built separately anywhere and this happens: the assistant path never passed --target cloudflare, and a Cloudflare course deployed to Netlify. Nothing failed; the site simply appeared on the wrong host. Netlify passes NO target flag at all — it is the launcher's default, and every course written before Cloudflare existed relies on that."
  },
